WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.920
Every support ticket starts with the same questions.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.775
What is this?

00:00:04.775 --> 00:00:05.893
How urgent is it?

00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:07.405
And who should take it?

00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:09.970
Support Triage answers them in seconds.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.190
A customer writes in.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.131
Before anyone opens it, the AI has read it.

00:00:18.131 --> 00:00:20.935
Category, priority, and the reason why.

00:00:20.935 --> 00:00:22.013
The right team.

00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:24.241
How frustrated the customer is.

00:00:24.241 --> 00:00:25.751
What's still missing.

00:00:25.751 --> 00:00:28.267
And a first reply, already drafted.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:31.430
Every run shows its model, and what it cost.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.285
Need the policy?

00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:35.646
Ask Sage, your private assistant.

00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:39.940
It answers from your own notes, and shows which one it used.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.121
The AI only suggests.

00:00:42.121 --> 00:00:47.338
An agent corrects it in one click, claims the ticket, and sends the reply.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:50.440
Nothing reaches a customer without a person.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:58.520
The queue keeps the team on time, with live response targets, urgent work first, and every action one click away.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.419
Prefer a board?

00:01:01.419 --> 00:01:02.520
Drag and drop.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.095
And it learns.

00:01:04.095 --> 00:01:10.920
Every correction becomes an example for the next similar ticket, and you can see exactly which ones it used.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:18.402
When many customers hit the same problem, it spots the incident, and drafts one update for all of them.

00:01:18.402 --> 00:01:20.710
Your team decides when it goes out.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:27.350
Analytics show response times, customer satisfaction, and whether the AI is getting better.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.665
Plus everything a modern help desk needs.

00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:33.610
Agents file tickets for customers who call in.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.300
Customers rate the help they got.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.550
Share a public status page for any ticket.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.380
Organise the work with team labels.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.580
Re-run the AI whenever you need to.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.730
Admins see the whole operation at a glance.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.090
Light and dark themes.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.990
It's secure by default,

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.880
with a clear privacy policy, and your data under your control.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:58.871
Support Triage.

00:01:58.871 --> 00:02:00.410
The AI does the reading.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.140
Your team does the helping.
